; prior: Clojure — `(when [] ...)` RUNS: empty collections are truthy; only
; nil and false are falsy.
; expectation: Loon agrees exactly, with None playing nil: [when #[] ...]
; runs its body.
; principle: where the prior is good, match it exactly (agent-first.md P1).
; expect-stdout: runs
[fn main []
  [when #[] [println "runs"]]]
